april's playstation plus games have been  confirmed and season 2 details for halo  infinite could be on the horizon  sony has officially confirmed the  playstation plus lineup for april 2022  with three more games coming to the  service from very different genres first  up is spongebob squarepants battle for  bikini bottom rehydrated and speaking of  hydration slip some water  right now this game is a remake of the  2003 platformer of the same name minus  the rehydrated part while the remake was  received rather poorly at least you  don't have to pay money for it now the  second game is hood outlaws and legends  an online multiplayer game that could be  aptly compared to payday except with a  medieval setting matches feature two  teams of four working towards stealing  treasure not only do you have to worry  about the other team but there are also  computer controlled enemies to contend  with the third free game is slayed  aspire a deck building game with  overarching roguelike systems this game  even earned a 9 out of 10 from us at  gamespot these games will be available  on the 6th of april so you have until  then to claim the free games from march  in other playstation plus news sony  announced that persona 5 will be leaving  the playstation plus collection on may  11. the company confirmed that players  will have until this date to add persona  5 to their library in order to continue  to access it while they have an active  playstation plus subscription and this  is the perfect time to remind you that  whenever a game is up on playstation  plus always hit add to library even if  you don't want to play the game i've had  persona 5 added to my library a long  time ago and i have absolutely no  interest so if you hate spongebob who  cares add it to your library anyway it's  a free game you might change your mind  in the future or just want to have  something for your nephew to play when  he comes over just just add it it's a  free game and if you missed it yesterday  sony revealed its brand new playstation  plus subscription service which will  launch in june with three new tiers the  standard subscription will be rebranded  to playstation plus essential and will  cost sixty dollars per year while  playstation plus extra will cost fifteen  dollars per month or a hundred dollars  per year and will feature 400 ps4 and  ps5 games the most expensive tier is  called playstation plus premium and will  cost 18 per month or 120 dollars per  year and it will include up to  340 additional games to that 400 i  mentioned earlier as well as cloud  streaming support but in news that has  nothing to do with playstation plus head  creative at 343 industries joseph  stadton says fans can expect new details  on what's next really soon during an  interview with the washington post  statin said quote fans are really soon  going to be exposed to some really cool  stuff we've got going for season 2. it's  taken a little bit longer to get the  engine up to speed communications  flowing in the way that we want to but  the engine is cranking and i'm super  excited about the next year and beyond  staten later clarified on twitter that  the engine he was referring to is not  halo infinite's game engine he was  instead using the word as a metaphor for  the whole halo infinite live service  during the interviews statin also  stressed that 343 industries wants fans  to be able to rely on whatever new  information the team puts out in regards  to halo infinite it's a sentiment statin  has echoed before like in february when  a planned status update on the state of  the game's upcoming co-op and forge  modes was delayed so that the team could  finalize plans and share reliable  information let me know in the comments  if you're still playing halo infinite  and how often is it like every night or  are we talking like  you know fortnight on mondays call of  duty on on wednesdays and halo just on  sunday nights let me know  [Music]
 

